# Tests Must Prove Behavior

- Test public contracts and security invariants, not implementation trivia.
- Every bug fix adds a failing regression test first or documents why reproduction requires an integration fixture.
- Do not mock the boundary under test. RLS, migrations, pgvector, LightRAG storage contracts, streaming resume, and container health require real integration tests.
- Frozen LLM fixtures are default; live-model tests are explicit, cost-capped, and never required for fast unit feedback.
- Assert positive behavior plus authorization denial, malformed input, timeout, budget exhaustion, cancellation, retry, idempotency, and fallback.
- Retrieval tests record ranked IDs and metrics; do not assert only that an answer string is non-empty.
- Chunk tests prove typed-element/heading/reading-order preservation, boilerplate decisions, 200–400-token distribution, atomic table/list handling, parent reconstruction, overlap bounds, citation coordinates, and exact/near-duplicate provenance.
- Hybrid tests separately score query-profile fields, Arabic index/query normalization, seeded code/alias recall, candidate-depth recall, always-versus-conditional top-20 OpenAI reranking with skipped-case counterfactuals, and query-class coverage/refusal curves.
- Keep embedding qualification, tuning/development, immutable launch holdout, and post-launch regression sets disjoint.
- Graph tests prove mapping coverage, current-version filtering, deletion/ACL suppression, no hidden keyword call, and bounded query work.
- Prompt-injection fixtures cover PDFs, crawled HTML, OCR, forged citations, tool instructions, graph poisoning, and frontend XSS.
- Security fixtures cover asymmetric JWKS rollover, upload MFA, stale malware signatures/re-scan, category/URL approval, egress denial, Valkey outage fallback, protected migration credentials, conversation deletion, audit-chain anchors, and origin-secret rotation.
- Load fixtures measure shared budget-row wait, event-loop lag/heartbeat jitter, maintenance-vs-query contention, embedding/index memory, and graph-writer throughput/ETA—not only request latency.
- A skipped required integration test is a failure. Jobs must fail when zero matching tests execute.
- Never use `|| true`, blanket exception suppression, arbitrary sleeps, or production auth bypasses.

## Test tiers

- PR: lint, types, unit/component, contracts, build.
- Main: migrations, RLS, integration, containers, focused E2E.
- Nightly/release: full E2E, retrieval evaluations, load, restart, deletion, restore, security, and live tests when explicitly enabled.
